    <string name="forget_failed">Sharepaste could not finish forgetting that Pairing.</string>

    <string name="pairings_add_heading">ADD ANOTHER PAIRING</string>
    <string name="pairings_add_body">A phone can hold several. Only the one marked Syncing is
        the one this phone sends to and receives from.</string>
    <string name="pairings_add_button">PAIR WITH A CODE</string>

    <!--
      One line per Pairing card, and the only cipher this product names
      anywhere: `core/crypto.rs` seals with XChaCha20-Poly1305.

      ADR 0002 asked for the disclosure beside pairing, where the choice to
      trust a Relay is being made. On this phone it is no longer there — the
      pairing flow's footer band went with the rest of its inert facts — so
      what survives is this card, which is read after the fact. A weaker
      placement than the ADR asked for, and recorded as such in ADR 0002.
    -->
    <string name="cipher_disclosure" translatable="false">XCHACHA20-POLY1305</string>

    <!--
      ===================================================================
      Settings, which are thinner here than on a computer. The reason is
      stated rather than left as a gap: someone who knows the desktop will
      come looking for the capture switch and the deny-list, and finding
      nothing is indistinguishable from finding a half-built screen.
      ===================================================================
    -->
    <string name="settings_heading">ABOUT THIS PHONE</string>
    <string name="settings_this_phone_heading">THIS PHONE</string>
    <!--
      The only switch on this screen. A Recall reaches the clipboard whichever
      way this is set; all it decides is whether the receipt names what arrived,
      which is the part a person may not want on screen in company. Capitals for
      the switch because it is a control, sentence case for what it means.
    -->
    <string name="settings_show_recalled">SHOW WHAT WAS RECALLED</string>
    <string name="settings_show_recalled_note">A Recall puts the Entry on the clipboard either
        way. This only decides whether Sharepaste tells you what it was.</string>
    <!--
      The two settings a computer has and a phone does not. Both are inert here
      rather than missing: `capture_enabled` governs Watched Capture, which a
      phone never performs (ADR 0007), and the deny-list matches a frontmost
      application, which a phone has no notion of.
    -->
    <string name="settings_absent_note">Your computer has two switches this phone does not.
        Sharepaste never watches this phone\u2019s clipboard — it only ever sends what you hand
        it — so there is nothing to turn on, and no list of apps to keep it away from.</string>
    <!--
      The same two, plus the update check, as chips. A chip that says N/A makes a
      missing switch legible as a decision; nothing at all makes it look like a
      screen somebody stopped building. `UPDATE CHECK · NONE` is ADR 0008: the
      phone carries no update code, so unlike a desktop it never asks an update
      source anything and the Relay is its only counterparty.
    -->
    <string name="settings_tag_watched_capture">WATCHED CAPTURE · N/A</string>
    <string name="settings_tag_deny_list">DENY-LIST · N/A</string>
    <string name="settings_tag_update_check">UPDATE CHECK · NONE</string>
</resources>
